WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
62% of women on glp-1s moved up a breast density category, driving extra mammogram callbacks. This is peptides weekly, episode 11, education and evidence, never dosing advice. After that mammogram comparison, a phase 3 weight result in children, a Toronto enforcement seizure, and this week's peptide spotlight on ghk. Brigham and women's radiologist Eva C. Gombos and colleagues lined up screening mammograms from before and after at least a year on a glp-1 receptor.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.320
after agonist used for weight loss, an observational before and after look rather than a randomized trial,

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:44.160
scheduled for the Radiological Society of North America meeting in Chicago from November 29th to December 3rd, 2026,

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:53.940
and not yet peer-reviewed in a journal. The name drugs include ozempic and wagovi. 107 women ages 34 to 79 lost anywhere

00:00:53.940 --> 00:01:01.920
from 6 pounds to 107, 40 on average across 214 scans, 8 women jumped to density categories,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.480
nobody in the set moved down, and everyday health, quoting Gombos, put the share class

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:12.920
as dense at a near tripling, about 15% before and about 42% after.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:18.400
Reuters' account of the same meeting report said density rose in every woman, and that

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.380
women who lost more weight showed a larger density rise.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:28.320
Reviewer to reviewer, smaller breasts showed up in roughly 58-79% and thicker skin in about

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.020
9-18%.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:37.120
Callbacks for more imaging hit 22.4% against an average US recall rate near 10%.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.080
Two of those callbacks were technical for positioning or the image itself.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.220
Four women went on to biopsy and all four results were benign.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:50.780
Gombos reads the pattern as fat leaving the breasts faster than the glandular tissue, so

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:55.120
So the picture looks denser even if the absolute amount of fibroglangular tissue falls.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.800
She and Melanie Chelman, a Cleveland Clinic breast radiologist, who was not on the study,

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:06.400
both say nobody yet knows whether this particular density rise changes long-term breast cancer

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:06.760
risk.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:12.820
Chelman adds that smaller, less fatty, denser breasts after weight loss are an old observation,

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:18.720
with or without a GLP1, and that the new part is how often large weight loss now happens.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:23.540
Gombos said the report is not a reason for patients to be alarmed about taking these

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:23.960
medicines.

00:02:25.068 --> 00:02:29.808
Nature Medicine's news note on the step-young trial says a phase three study found children

00:02:29.808 --> 00:02:34.948
with obesity lost significantly more weight on semi-glutide than on placebo, and that

00:02:34.948 --> 00:02:39.068
more than one third landed at a body mass index under the obesity cutoff.

00:02:39.568 --> 00:02:44.588
Sample size, dose, and side effect counts are not in that note, so they stay out of this

00:02:44.588 --> 00:02:44.948
telling.

00:02:44.948 --> 00:02:50.488
CBC reports that health Canada sees peptides from a Toronto shop and warned about health

00:02:50.488 --> 00:02:56.088
risks in the unregulated market, an enforcement step beyond earlier warnings rather than a trial

00:02:56.088 --> 00:03:02.748
of any named peptides effect. Tech Time says Duke has signed onto an LSA-LT peptide trial aimed

00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:07.768
at kidney injury around heart surgery, and that a genin-tech study hosted there ended early.

00:03:08.248 --> 00:03:12.208
That is a site joining a study, not a published patient result for the peptide.

00:03:12.208 --> 00:03:18.708
Drug Topics on November 19, 2026, described patients and prescribers flooding pharmacies

00:03:18.708 --> 00:03:23.768
with peptide questions, and an expert casting the pharmacist's job as turning that confusion

00:03:23.768 --> 00:03:26.888
into counseling. Practice report, not a trial.

00:03:27.628 --> 00:03:32.908
Bioengineer.org headlines an observational study tying GLP-1 therapy to less pain

00:03:32.908 --> 00:03:37.888
and a smaller circumference in lipidema, with no further measurements in the text at hand.

00:03:37.888 --> 00:03:43.908
J.D. Super reports Kentucky holding the line on peptide compounding, a legal stance rather

00:03:43.908 --> 00:03:45.088
than a clinical result.

00:03:45.548 --> 00:03:50.968
The Royal Australian College of General Practitioners reports a national peptide's inquiry that

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:53.168
will look at vertically integrated telehealth.

00:03:54.112 --> 00:03:59.532
GHK, this week's spotlight, is a human tripeptide of glycine, histidine, and lysine.

00:04:00.192 --> 00:04:05.892
Glycel L. histidil L. lysine, and a 2018 review in the International Journal of Molecular

00:04:05.892 --> 00:04:12.132
sciences carries the copper-bound name GHK-CU in its title, while the abstracts claims

00:04:12.132 --> 00:04:17.372
are written for the peptide itself. Those papers never state a drug approval, a trial phase,

00:04:17.592 --> 00:04:23.672
or a cosmetic authorization. The review says GHK stimulates blood vessel and nerve outgrowth,

00:04:24.192 --> 00:04:30.412
raises synthesis of collagen, elastin, and glycosaminoglycans, and supports dermal fibroblasts.

00:04:30.412 --> 00:04:34.552
Collagen and Alastin are the structural proteins of connective tissue.

00:04:35.352 --> 00:04:39.092
Glycosamino glycans are the sugar chains that hold water in that matrix.

00:04:39.972 --> 00:04:42.152
Fibroblasts are cells that build much of it.

00:04:42.612 --> 00:04:46.992
On that telling, the peptide is a signal to repair machinery the tissue already has.

00:04:47.452 --> 00:04:48.952
Not a filler parked in the skin.

00:04:49.652 --> 00:04:56.632
The abstract says improved repair has been demonstrated in skin, lung connective tissue, bone, liver, and stomach lining.

00:04:56.632 --> 00:05:01.372
and it does not split those demonstrations into cell, animal, or human work.

00:05:01.852 --> 00:05:06.352
The authors, writing from what they call current knowledge, also list actions they treat

00:05:06.352 --> 00:05:07.352
as health positive.

00:05:07.972 --> 00:05:13.972
Several anti-cancer activities, anti-inflammatory effects, lung protection, restoration of

00:05:13.972 --> 00:05:20.352
fibroblasts taken from chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, suppression of NF-CAPAB, which they

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:26.012
describe as a molecule thought to speed diseases of aging, plus effects they label anti-anxiety,

00:05:26.012 --> 00:05:31.512
antibody, anti-pain, and anti-aggression, DNA repair, and switching on cell cleansing through

00:05:31.512 --> 00:05:34.732
the proteasome, the cell's protein disposal system.

00:05:35.212 --> 00:05:40.812
They suggest gene data may explain the spread, because GHK looks as if it regulates multiple

00:05:40.812 --> 00:05:42.172
biochemical pathways.

00:05:42.752 --> 00:05:47.892
That is a review reading gene findings, not a new count of people, wrinkles, wounds, or

00:05:47.892 --> 00:05:48.332
cancers.

00:05:49.092 --> 00:05:53.032
The other paper is from 1983, and it is not a GHK experiment.

00:05:53.032 --> 00:06:00.372
In the test tube, L ascorbic acid plus copper 2 ion, or plus a copper 2 tripeptide, cuts

00:06:00.372 --> 00:06:03.032
several viral DNAs and proteins extensively.

00:06:03.632 --> 00:06:09.232
The tripeptide was diglissal L histidine, a copper binding 3 amino acid peptide of the

00:06:09.232 --> 00:06:12.572
same general kind, not identified there as GHK.

00:06:13.192 --> 00:06:15.052
A scorbate alone did nothing apparent.

00:06:15.632 --> 00:06:18.072
The copper tripeptide alone did nothing apparent.

00:06:18.072 --> 00:06:23.092
Of the transition metals tried with a scorebait, copper and iron were the most effective.

00:06:23.672 --> 00:06:28.212
Catalase, which breaks down hydrogen peroxide, partly blocked the DNA cutting.

00:06:28.852 --> 00:06:30.732
Superoxide dismutase did not.

00:06:31.392 --> 00:06:36.092
The authors read that as hydrogen peroxide in the pathway, and they say one product is

00:06:36.092 --> 00:06:39.132
probably the hydroxyl radical made from that peroxide.

00:06:39.752 --> 00:06:44.652
Among reducing agents they tried, a scorebait was the strongest at cutting DNA and protein.

00:06:44.652 --> 00:06:50.032
cell-free chemistry on viral material, not a human safety trial, and not a test

00:06:50.032 --> 00:06:55.152
of a cosmetic cream. What is missing is the human wrong. These abstracts never say

00:06:55.152 --> 00:06:59.852
how many people receive GHK or GHKCU. They never show a randomized

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:05.032
comparison of a copper peptide cream against a plain cream. Anti-cancer language in

00:07:05.032 --> 00:07:10.092
a review summary is not fewer cancers in patients. The 1983 cleavage is not

00:07:10.092 --> 00:07:14.452
shown to occur in living skin, and it is not shown to be irrelevant there either.

00:07:14.452 --> 00:07:19.772
A list of repair pathways is not a drug claim, and nothing in these papers shows a product

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.752
label matching a measured human result.

00:07:22.232 --> 00:07:27.232
The risk that is actually measured is narrow and chemical, a related copper tripeptide

00:07:27.232 --> 00:07:33.392
quiet by itself in that assay, cut viral DNA and protein once ascorbate was added, on

00:07:33.392 --> 00:07:36.472
a peroxide route the authors tie to the hydroxyl radical.

00:07:37.072 --> 00:07:40.472
That is a reason not to hear copper peptide as automatically gentle.

00:07:40.472 --> 00:07:44.792
It is not a dose, a protocol, or a reason to start or stop anything.

00:07:45.532 --> 00:07:50.252
Contamination of unregulated products is a separate problem these two papers do not document.

00:07:51.295 --> 00:07:55.675
One thing worth knowing from the human evidence is that a density category change on paired

00:07:55.675 --> 00:08:01.155
mammograms can alter a screening picture after GLP1 weight loss without answering whether

00:08:01.155 --> 00:08:02.375
cancer risk moved.

00:08:02.855 --> 00:08:07.975
Another is that a phase 3 trial in children with obesity separated somaglutide from placebo

00:08:07.975 --> 00:08:13.435
on weight, with more than a third crossing under the obesity line on body mass index, which

00:08:13.435 --> 00:08:18.755
is a trial result and not an instruction. That's peptides weekly. This show is education,

00:08:19.035 --> 00:08:24.295
not medical advice. Talk to your own clinician before acting on anything you heard. I'm Patrick

00:08:24.295 --> 00:08:29.695
in Vancouver. See you next week. A rating on Apple podcasts or Spotify takes 10 seconds,

